{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083756-conditions-and-beat-suggestions","id":1083756,"title":"Conditions and Beat Suggestions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-25T17:17:27-07:00","id":1083756,"title":"Conditions and Beat Suggestions","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So, I am trying to get a good amount of beats for my players and I have been struggling with coming up with good ways to go about this while telling the story. I have recently placed the Amnesia Condition on the characters as their minds were wiped by the God-Machine when they turned down its offer for power. This has awarded 1-2 beats per character per session as they encounter something that reminds them of their past life, but I know that this cannot last forever so I was looking for some suggestions on how to incorporate more Conditions whether negative or positive.<br /> <br /> We are playing a Geist game using the GMC rule update, but I felt that since this is just a general question I have placed it in this area of the forum. The main themes around the game are Mystery and Horror of the Unknown.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if anyone else had suffered with the same kind of dilemma in regards to giving the characters enough chances to earn beats per session so they can advance their character long and make the story more interesting.<br /> <br /> I have toyed around with giving beats when the characters unlock clues, but that is a system I have yet to tackle since it seems very abstract and I am having trouble piecing that system together well enough to use it.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T17:23:02-07:00","id":1083758,"title":"","content":"If they're getting 1-2 per session for a Persistent Condition, then 1-2 for following Aspirations, and one for Dramatic Failures, one more for showing up, that should be an Experience per session, which is more than fair.<br /> <br /> Divvying beats out works best when both ST and the players working together. If the ST wants it mostly in their hands, then they're going to have to ply to the Aspirations a lot and have the players encounter things that give them Conditions. If the players want it and their ST isn't assisting, they're going to need reasonable Aspirations and to take opportunity of situations that grant Conditions, such as Breaking Points, Exceptional Successes and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-25-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T17:40:42-07:00","id":1083762,"title":"","content":"My advice for handing out Conditions, especially if you are running a game from a 1e sourcebook with the GMC updates, is that pretty much everything that leaves a floating bonus, penalty, or other lingering effect, should be in the form of a Condition. If a Condition doesn't already exist that approximates the lingering effect in question, improvise a new one. Have notecards on hand so you can jot down the effects of any new Conditions you improvise and hand them to the character that gets them. If you don't already have Mage 2e, it's worth getting even if you don't have immediate plans to run Mage because it has great advice on creating new Conditions that I really wish could have been in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:18:07-07:00","id":1085555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1083756-conditions-and-beat-suggestions?p=1083762#post1083762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice for handing out Conditions, especially if you are running a game from a 1e sourcebook with the GMC updates, is that pretty much everything that leaves a floating bonus, penalty, or other lingering effect, should be in the form of a Condition. If a Condition doesn't already exist that approximates the lingering effect in question, improvise a new one. Have notecards on hand so you can jot down the effects of any new Conditions you improvise and hand them to the character that gets them. If you don't already have Mage 2e, it's worth getting even if you don't have immediate plans to run Mage because it has great advice on creating new Conditions that I really wish could have been in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Couldn't like the pdf version be updated on Drivethrurpg with it though? It seems like a really simple fix of something that should be included in the Core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:32:35-07:00","id":1085588,"title":"","content":"OPP doesn't do updates on existing products once the final version comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=